WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.932
GPT-style models use decoder-only architecture and autoregressive next-token prediction.

00:00:05.932 --> 00:00:13.967
Give the model a prefix such as “natural language processing is,” and it predicts a distribution over what

00:00:13.967 --> 00:00:17.497
token might come next. Repeating that process produces longer text.

00:00:17.497 --> 00:00:24.862
Chat models build on this capability with instruction tuning, preference optimization, conversation templates,

00:00:24.862 --> 00:00:28.527
safety training, or other post-training methods.

00:00:28.527 --> 00:00:32.897
A generative model can also reason over text you provide in the prompt, summarize context,

00:00:32.897 --> 00:00:36.422
or answer questions about it.

00:00:36.422 --> 00:00:41.257
But it is important to separate language generation from information storage.

00:00:41.257 --> 00:00:47.237
A decoder model is not automatically a current database, a private document repository,

00:00:47.237 --> 00:00:49.417
or a verified source system.

00:00:49.417 --> 00:00:55.972
That distinction is one reason RAG becomes useful: retrieval supplies external evidence,

00:00:55.972 --> 00:00:59.401
while the decoder uses that evidence to generate a response.
